the diplomatic rift between the US and  Britain is growing wider over  embarrassing leaked cables critical of  President Trump British ambassador Kim  Derrick was uninvited from a dinner the  president attended last night earlier  mr. Trump said the US would no longer  deal with Derrick in the cables the  Ambassador called the Trump  administration inept Ben Tracy is at the  White House Ben Britain is supposed to  be our closest ally how big a deal is  this well the president is clearly  annoyed and the British government is  launching an investigation into who  leaked these memos now they say that the  UK says its ambassadors are supposed to  be candid that they're supposed to send  their thoughts back to British officials  but the content of these leaked memos is  painfully blunt in one of them  ambassador Kim Derrick writes we don't  really believe Trump's administration is  going to become substantially more  normal less dysfunctional less  diplomatically clumsy and inept in  another he says president Trump radiates  insecurity now the president responded  Monday on Twitter saying the Ambassador  is not liked or well thought of within  the US and then bluntly said we will no  longer deal with him outgoing Prime  Minister Theresa May says she still  supports Derek but the British  government says it is made clear to the  US how unfortunate all of this is it  does come at a critical time when both  the US and the UK face a new threat from  Iran which just yesterday further  exceeded its uranium enrichment cap  bringing it closer to developing a  nuclear weapon now after the u.s. pulled  out of that nuclear deal the remaining  European members have been trying to  keep Iran in side the agreement Anthony  meanwhile been the president gave a  speech yesterday boasting about his  administration's environmental record  how does this record actually measure up  well the President did position himself  as a champion of the environment he said  that the US can really lead on fighting  air in water pollution around the world  but keep in mind it was the president  that pulled out of the Paris climate  Accord and has overseen sweeping  rollbacks of air and water protections  now the president previously called for  the Environmental Protection Agency to  be eliminated which is why some green  groups are calling his speech yesterday  utter  we should also point out that during  that 20 minute speech there were two  words that the president never said and  those words are climate change Anthony  all right then thank you very much
 

